# Placeholder so the empty MacOS/ directory is tracked in git.
#
# This is the source-of-truth skeleton for /Applications/Pincer.app.
# It deliberately lives under `scripts/PincerBundle/` (NOT a
# `.app` suffix) so macOS LaunchServices on developer machines does
# not index it as a second installed app with the `io.github.modcritic.pincer`
# bundle id. With the previous `scripts/Pincer.app/` shape, every
# `cargo run` from inside the repo would surface a "ghost Pincer"
# entry in System Settings → Privacy & Security pointing at the empty
# skeleton path.
#
# At build / install time the pincer release binary (universal
# macOS slice — arm64 + x86_64 lipo'd together) is copied into this
# directory as `pincer`. The Info.plist's CFBundleExecutable
# points at that name.
#
# In upstream Cua (neither file is part of this fork):
#   - .github/workflows/cd-rust-pincer.yml  (copies the skeleton's
#     Contents/ into the release tarball at CD time and adds the
#     universal binary)
#   - libs/cua-driver/scripts/install.sh        (downloads the
#     resulting tarball, extracts it to /Applications/Pincer.app,
#     and creates the ~/.local/bin/pincer symlink pointing into
#     the bundle)
